<p>Iran’s state media say Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi has traveled to Geneva for a second round of indirect talks with the United States, after an earlier round in Oman last week. The talks are expected to take place on Tuesday, with Oman again serving as mediator, according to Iran’s state-run IRNA news agency.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/IehXhBQ3E-rg8ojikSjnrHnCZ84NnPy83yuk1X4PEhsr5jzpHYjTvHd9NktSzu5r254hwnwC2kbVxY876JZnKvmqj4uikIoK_C1ExmkmjddrZ3kjT47VUfrAKA3XphIY_CwROtBtzmRs9xAy1lWycZOCs_CLKvj3AoOUg985vEtkOjRbX1Gk86FWSwyseCOa8aIfA91rmEiK2LbzW526Z6aqOE8UCZlm9lOu01pol_vbOYMrYAHg9fUTQOFxjsVzRoypOStwGntwQWT5Gg' alt='U.S. special envoy Steve Witkoff, Jared Kushner and Oman&#x27;s Foreign Minister Badr bin Hamad al-Busaidi during a meeting in Muscat on Feb. 6.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>State-media rollout: SCMP reports that IRNA previewed the Geneva round in a Telegram post, and Iranian state TV later said Araghchi had arrived in the Swiss city.</li><li>US pressure backdrop: SCMP says Washington is keeping up pressure on Iran even as the indirect talks resume.</li><li>Negotiation aims: A diplomat quoted by The Globe and Mail said Iran is seeking a “mutually beneficial” nuclear deal with the United States.</li><li>Revival framing: Firstpost describes the new Geneva round as part of an effort to restart negotiations over the nuclear file.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Iranian state media (IRNA/state TV): Iranian outlets promoted the Geneva round through official channels, with IRNA previewing the next steps and state TV reporting that Araghchi is in Geneva. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/middle-east/article/3343656/irans-top-diplomat-attend-indirect-talks-us-geneva-state-news-says'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>Iranian government/diplomat (via Globe and Mail): A diplomat said Iran is seeking a “mutually beneficial” nuclear deal with the United States as the new round of talks approaches. (<a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-iran-us-nuclear-talks-tehran/'>The Globe and Mail</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/irans-state-media-reports-foreign-minister-will-attend-indirect-talks-with-the-u-s'>Iran&#x27;s state media reports foreign minister will attend indirect talks with the U.S.</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/middle-east/article/3343656/irans-top-diplomat-attend-indirect-talks-us-geneva-state-news-says'>Iran’s foreign minister in Geneva for second round of high-stakes talks with US</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-iran-us-nuclear-talks-tehran/'>Iran pursuing mutually beneficial nuclear deal with U.S., diplomat says</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/irans-abbas-araghchi-departs-for-geneva-for-second-round-of-us-nuclear-talks-13980110.html'>Iran’s Abbas Araghchi departs for Geneva for second round of US nuclear talks</a> - firstpost.com</li></ul>